A simple way to detect battery charge with reasonable accuracy. Here the end of charging is detected when the battery voltage reaches 13.6V (-200mV from the supply voltage) and the current at that time is ~133mA, then the red LED goes off. The uniqueness of me idea is the reduction of the base opening voltage threshold by adding a dropout voltage on R2 resistor from voltage divider of  R2 + R3.
The voltage supposedly reduces the base opening voltage of the transistor from ~600mV to ~200mV. This is achieved by adding a 400mV difference to the transistor base. A 0.4V voltage is created with a divider from R2+R3 resistors.
